  "seoTitle": "Delhi Smog and Data Concerns After Deepavali",
  "metaDescription": "New Delhi faces severe air pollution after Deepavali as concerns emerge regarding the accuracy of government air quality data monitoring systems.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "New Delhi experienced its highest air pollution levels in five years following Deepavali firecracker use.",
    "Multiple government air quality monitoring stations went offline during peak pollution periods.",
    "Analysts and political parties have raised questions regarding the accuracy and reporting of official air quality index data."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Following the Deepavali festival, New Delhi has been covered by a thick layer of smog, with air quality reaching severe levels. This seasonal pollution crisis has intensified as recent fireworks contributed to the hazardous conditions. A significant point of contention has emerged regarding the integrity of government monitoring infrastructure, as numerous official air quality stations ceased reporting data during the period of peak pollution. Experts from the Centre for Research on Energy and Clean Air noted that missing hourly PM2.5 data could artificially deflate reported Air Quality Index figures. Private monitoring agencies have reported significantly higher pollution levels than official government sources, leading to political friction. Various political entities are now debating the potential for data manipulation or system failures, while observers express concern over the transparency of the current air quality assessment process in the capital.",
